  "episode_summary": "James Staples and Luke Heslop travel to Brick Lane in East London to explore the history of Bangladeshi migration through food. They meet Dr. Ashraf Hoque and restaurant owner Shanur Mai at Gram Bangla, where they discuss the migration of Sylheti communities, the origins of Bengali restaurants in Britain, East London's multicultural history, and authentic Bangladeshi cuisine. The episode highlights how food preserves identity, memory, and community among migrants while examining the evolution of Bengali restaurants in the UK.",
